  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decreasing the burden of TB in Romania through reforming the TB control system and strengthening the management of drug resistant forms of TB by ensuring universal access to DR-TB diagnosis and treatment and addressing the needs of populati - Romania (01-Apr-2015-30-Sep-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Romania, Tuberculosis, Romanian Angel Appeal Foundation (RAA)This program has the following goals: To contribute to the achievement of reduction of TB incidence and mortality in Romania through improved hight impact intervention (diagnosis, treatment, care and prevention) with special focus on key affected populations.. The objectives of this program are: Addressing the needs in TB prevention, diagnosis, treatment and care of key affected population through implementation of a patient centered interventions in 6 high TB burden counties in Romania.  Contributing to early and quality assured TB diagnosis through the strengthening of TB laboratory capacity.  Contributing to the improvement of treatment outcomes for M/XDR TB patients by provision of complete, non-interrupted drug regimens.  Strengthening the national legal framework to regulate the TB control in Romania</narrative>
  </description>
